Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||12-13-2001||05:54 PM||||didja know... that in some parts of the world, a simple elevation change can make that drastic of a difference?  I was in Scotland years ago (2nd trip of 3) and climbed Ben Nevis (highest peak in GB- only about 5K<FONT SIZE="1">?</FONT> feet vertical though).  Anyway- the temp at the base was nearly 80 degrees F.  By the time we reached the peak, it had dropped to about 30 degrees and I had the joy of having a snowball fight- in June!  Anything is possible. <P>And I don't really think that's the point anyway. Do you really think the stuff we see on CNN and the news is the way it really is?  I certainly don't think so... yes, the certainly could be a bunch of BS- but again, I don't really think that's the point.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||12-13-2001||06:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>didja know... that in some parts of the world, a simple elevation change can make that drastic of a difference?  I was in Scotland years ago (2nd trip of 3) and climbed Ben Nevis (highest peak in GB- only about 5K<FONT SIZE="1">?</FONT> feet vertical though).  Anyway- the temp at the base was nearly 80 degrees F.  By the time we reached the peak, it had dropped to about 30 degrees and I had the joy of having a snowball fight- in June!  Anything is possible. <P>And I don't really think that's the point anyway. Do you really think the stuff we see on CNN and the news is the way it really is?  I certainly don't think so... yes, the certainly could be a bunch of BS- but again, I don't really think that's the point.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, it sure it does make difference... but the fact of the matter is that the story is flawed. I don't believe that it was writen by anyone near the action, or in a position to comment about it. Sounds to me like someone doesn't like afghanis.... I don't think you'd like to be called a hun, either... it's a racist document, written by someone with a lot to say, cowardly hiding behind your military. your people are busting their asses off out there. they don't need this kind os  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"><P>but yes, we don't see what's really going on. It just makes me sick to see all this BS floating around. things like the shopping mall on Oct. 31... stuff like that. It's sadistic, and vile.<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||12-13-2001||06:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>...your people are busting their asses off out there. they don't need this kind of   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"><P>but yes, we don't see what's really going on. It just makes me sick to see all this BS floating around. things like the shopping mall on Oct. 31... stuff like that. It's sadistic, and vile.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Agreed.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Mach10||12-13-2001||06:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B> Agreed.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>oh, and Scotland rules  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> only been to the south border... but the highlands are just Beautiful  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Yeah, I've been mountain hiking before, and gone above snow-line. You don't find many cold-blooded invertebrates at that altitude. the caves being refered to are (to my understanding) at the foot-hills. afghanistan is in winter-mode right now, so the average temperature is probably below -2ºC... that's colder than any insect that *I* know of being able to survive outside of larval and hibernation mechanisms... I could be wrong, but it's STILL fishy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||12
Z||000010||maryjane||12-14-2001||01:44 AM||||Formula 88- I read this a week or so ago on a USMC Vietnam helicopters association website. Also read your "One Marine" joke there. The letter is supposedly from a Bill Hanna. It may be a genuine article, I dunno, but the first time I read it, it just didn't read right. Afganistan is a pretty backwards country right now. Radios are few, television extremely rare. How would a combat Marine ( sounds like force recon or Forward Air Control) out in the boonies for months know in detail what CNN is showing on their nightly broadcasts? Mach 10 is correct about the bugs. Chiggers, fleas, and scorpions in a place where you have to cover your snow tracks? It's ben bantered back & forth by email among members of Popasmoke, the name of the heicopter assn,; general feeling is, it's a fraud. I even went back & reread some my old letters from viet nam (my mother saved every one I wrote as a young Marine), the whole thing just doesn't 'feel' right. It's far too well written to be from a combat Marine sitting in a hole somewhere in the middle of nowhere. All that perfect puntuation? c'mon.  just my opinion.  <A HREF="http://www.popasmoke.com/cgi-bin/readyroom.cgi?read=3393" TARGET=_blank>http://www.popasmoke.com/cgi-bin/readyroom.cgi?read=3393</A> <p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 12-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula88||12-14-2001||10:45 AM||||Well, like I said, I can't verify it's accuracy.  But to be honest, I don't really think that detracts from the statement.  I shared this because I found it thought provoking, but not really intending to start a debate.<P>I'm not going to defend it's accuracy, because I can't.  If you think it's a bunch of <I>BlackStang</I>, that's your option.<P>To be honest the only paragrath that's really important, IMO, is the last one.  It may not have been written in the field by a member of the military, but I still agree with it.||||reg||3
Z||000012||Tonker||12-14-2001||11:07 AM||||I have my doubts about how <I>real</I> it is, too, but that's really not the point of it. What I get from it is an indictment of how people over here are too involved in the <I>show</I> of the war and less on the issues that are really affecting America(and the rest of the world) now. We're definately beeing fleeced, to a certain extent, by the media. This is big bucks for them. I think he's suggesting that rather than accepting everything you hear from Aaron Brown and Co, take it with a grain of salt. Everybody is so pre-occupied with the "sexy news" from the Middle East that we're not paying as much attention to the other issues affecting us as we should.<P>It could have been written by by someone over there, I understand that some of the special forces guys and marines are pretty well educated. My guess is it was someone who wanted to make a point and used a fictional character to deliver it. Just read it and take from it what you will. I thought it was an interesting story, personally.<P>Just my $0.02, keep the change.<p>[This message has been edited by Tonker (edited 12-14-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000013||Mach10||12-14-2001||11:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B><P>I'm not going to defend it's accuracy, because I can't.  If you think it's a bunch of <I>BlackStang</I>, that's your option.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>*snicker*<BR>*snort*<BR>ROFL<P>Good one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Yeah, the last paragraph is pretty righteous... My point about people trying to feed of this situation stands though... We've seen WAY too much of this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||maryjane||12-14-2001||12:10 PM||||Didn't really mean to fuel a debate. I would like to think it is authentic. & I agree the news media way overplays things just for sensationalism & ratings, especially CNN. Being the war-mongering, hateful, old sob that I am, I eat all that stuff up, but even I have my fill of it. And thank's for posting it 88, I was going to, but didn't want to do all that typing. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. Never have figured that copy/paste thing.||||reg||1
Z||000015||isthiswhereiputausername?||12-14-2001||01:07 PM||||It does have a lot of valid points on it. <P>As far as him talking about the news reporters, some of the guys on MSNBC news dont have a FREAKING clue! <P>Their homeland security guy on that show is a joke.  I never once saw such a moron on TV until I heard him talking about "security". <BR>His idea of the threat to the US is CANADA!?!?!   "we need to close & secure our borders against Canada",   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fwtf.gif">   and goes on talking about how much of the borders are open and easy for terrorists to enter.   Ummm last time I checked.. we were on thE US's Side?  AND there are US immergration posted at all checkpoints.<P>Sometime your REALLY bored.. sit down and watch msnbc.. there are a few on there that would make you sit there and think <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fwtf.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>On MSNBC news, both him and that bigheaded loud freak who wont let his interviewees get a sentence out before he interrupts them for some reason should be sent over to afghanistan as cave bait   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by isthiswhereiputausername? (edited 12-14-2001).]||||reg||1
